# secrets.schema: every secret this project uses, by name. Committed; it never holds a value.
# Values live encrypted in the secrets repo of the project's owner (<PROJECT>/ in it; make secrets-doctor names it)
# and reach a command only through its environment (`make` does this for you). Add a line here, then `make secrets-init` or
# `make secrets-set NAME=... ENV=...`.
#
# Columns, separated by spaces:
#   NAME         the variable name (or, for envs=keys, the key file name: keys/<NAME>.sops)
#   envs         comma list of common local staging production, or `keys` for a signing key file
#   used-by      comma list of who needs it: cf (a Worker secret, pushed by `make cf-secrets`),
#                auth (a credential the tooling itself uses, such as the Cloudflare token; never
#                pushed to a Worker), ci (CI jobs), local (`make dev`), firmware, app
#   gen          no (asked for), a byte count (random base64url, `make secrets-init GEN=1`), or for
#                keys a keygen type: ed25519 ecdsa-p256 rsa-3072 mcuboot-ecdsa-p256 espsecure-v2
#   description  the rest of the line
#
# NAME                 envs                       used-by        gen   description
